    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "Find the smallest four-digit number that is divisible by 5 and 9.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$1035$; the smallest four-digit multiple of $45$.",
      "worked": "Using the largest power of each prime,\n$$\\begin{align*}5 &= 3^0\\times5^1\\\\9 &= 3^2\\times5^0\\\\\\operatorname{LCM}(5,9) &= 3^2\\times5^1=45\\end{align*}$$\nThe required number is a multiple of $45$.\n$$\\begin{align*}45\\times22 &= 990\\\\45\\times23 &= 1035\\end{align*}$$\nSince $990$ has three digits and $1035$ has four digits, the smallest four-digit number divisible by both $5$ and $9$ is $1035$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
